# Quizzy

Quizzy is a Rails 8 app for preparing conference quizzes. The moderator area is at `/moderate`; `/up` is the public health check.

## Run

Set `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `QUIZZY_MODERATOR_USERNAME` and `QUIZZY_MODERATOR_PASSWORD`, then run `bin/serve`. It prepares the production SQLite database in `storage/`, precompiles the local design assets, and starts Puma on all interfaces (`PORT`, default 3000). The server uses plain HTTP; restrict access to a trusted network or terminate TLS upstream when sending moderator credentials.

## Data and preview

Quizzes own ordered questions. Each question stores its text options and correctness flags as one ordered JSON array so an edit succeeds or fails as a unit. Preview uses the active questions in that order; choices and score live only in the current browser page, with no answer requests, cookies or local storage used to record them.

Run `bin/rails test` for the Rails test suite.
